{"text": " Assalamualaikum warahmatullahi wabarakatuh. Hi, I'm Abu Zahmat, a software engineer and co-founder of Team RealMetallus. Our project Be Better is an award-winning AI fitness application developed for the smart health hackathon powered by StartAD by NYU and Department of Health Abu Dhabi, where we won first place. Today, millions of our people exercise without proper feedback. They may perform movements incorrectly, build unsafe habits or only realize something is wrong after pain or injury appears. Be Better asks a foresight question, what if the gym of the future could prevent injury before it happens? Be Better uses AI, computer vision and variable data concepts to give real-time posture correction and adaptive training feedback. Instead of generic workout advice, Be Better helps users understand how they move, correct mistakes instantly and train in a safer, more personalized way. It is designed for a future where gyms, schools, workplaces and community wellness spaces can offer intelligent preventive coaching to everyone. Over the next 10 years, Be Better can help shift fitness from reactive treatment to proactive prevention. This means fewer preventable injuries, safer exercise habits and better access to guidance for people who cannot always afford a personal trainer or specialist support. Our vision is not only to build an app but to help shape a future where everyday movement becomes smarter, safer and more human-centered. Be Better shows how foresight, AI and human-centered design can come together to improve well-being before problems begin. We are team members and our mission is simple, help people move better, train safer and build a healthier future. Thank you.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 5.84, "text": " Assalamualaikum warahmatullahi wabarakatuh. Hi, I'm Abu Zahmat, a software engineer and co-founder", "tokens": [50364, 6281, 23819, 901, 64, 35518, 1516, 545, 15677, 858, 27783, 261, 455, 23346, 267, 3232, 13, 242